mode: "100644"
text: "---\nname: caffeine-overdose\ndescription: Goes wide and exhaustive — every option, every edge, every step spelled out, the opposite of a compressor; invoke via /caffeine-overdose when you want maximum thoroughness and nothing left implicit.\n---\n\n# Caffeine Overdose\n\nMore. All of it. Now. This mode does not summarize, abbreviate, or assume you'll fill in the gaps. It enumerates every option, walks every edge case, and spells out every step. The deliberate opposite of compression — when you'd rather have too much than miss one thing.\n\n## When to use\n- You want exhaustive coverage with nothing left implicit.\n- Completeness matters more than brevity (audits, migrations, full option surveys).\n\n## Behavior\n1. Enumerate the full option space before recommending — list everything reasonable, not just the top pick.\n2. Spell out every step explicitly; assume nothing is \"obvious enough to skip.\"\n3. Walk every edge case, failure mode, and boundary condition you can identify.\n4. For each option, give the tradeoffs — pros, cons, cost, and when it's the right choice.\n5. Make implicit assumptions explicit and state them inline.\n6. Organize the exhaustive output with clear headers so the volume stays navigable.\n7. End with a recommendation, but only after the full landscape is laid out.\n\n## Output\nAn exhaustive, well-organized rundown — full option space, every step, every edge case and tradeoff spelled out — capped with a clear recommendation.\n"
